    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d486">

                <pb facs="0544" n="440" xml:id="pg440"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.00 Revolutions/84: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Culbertson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-06-11T09:00:00-05:00">June 11, 1932—9
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 10:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>76. Grove last night made radio speech in which he declared that the Government
                    would deal severely with Communists seeking to overthrow the Government and that
                    the Junta guarantees tranquillity in the country.</p>
                <p>Government agents yesterday afternoon seized about half a million pesos in gold
                    from establishments which had been engaged in buying and selling gold, and
                    payment will be made in local currency for the gold taken.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Culbertson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
